+## Independent verification (re-derived, not reporter-supplied)
+
+- **FINDING 1 — band/threshold equivalence, confirmed.** With C(n)=ceil(log2 n!),
+  D(n)=S(n)-C(n), B={(1^n,bin(c)) : D(n)<=c}: C(n) is poly-computable from unary n and
+  S(n)<=n(n-1)/2 is kernel-checked, so D(n)<n^2/2. (=>) SORT-BOUND-U(1^n#1^k): reject if
+  k<C(n), accept if k>=n(n-1)/2, else ONE query B(1^n,bin(k-C(n))) decides S(n)<=k with
+  c<=n(n-1)/2-C(n) of poly bit-length. (<=) B(1^n,bin(c)): if c>=n(n-1)/2-C(n) accept;
+  else form k=C(n)+c in unary (size O(n^2)) and query SORT-BOUND-U(1^n#1^k). Hence
+  B in P iff SORT-BOUND-U in P. The fixed-c/nonuniform-in-c caveat is correct: such a
+  family cannot be scanned over c=0..O(n^2) to yield S in FP.
+- **FINDING 2 — conditional, correct as labeled.** D(n) in {0,1} for n<=22 matches C(n)
+  and known S(n); Sergeev (ECCC TR20-096) gives only D(n)=o(n), which does not refute
+  D(n)<=1 for all n. Under that unrefuted hypothesis BAND_1 is trivial while
+  BAND_0 =_T^p S(n); so BAND_1 =_T^p S(n) implies (D unbounded) or (S in FP). The failed
+  S(n)-to-BAND_1 reduction is a genuine obstruction (one-bit D(m)<=1 answers are
+  uninformative when D(n)>=2), not an equivalence proof.
+- Model-fidelity notes check out: general-poset hardness does not transfer to the fixed
+  antichain root without a reduction; soundness is not completeness; many-one sparsity
+  (Mahaney) does not rule out a tally Turing-oracle equivalence.
+
+## Disposition
